However, we must still be explicit about the type of the pinned reference; otherwise, Rust will
still not know to interpret these as dynamic trait objects, which is what we need them to be in
the Vec . We therefore add pin to our list of imports from std::pin . Then we can pin! each
future when we define it and define futures as a Vec containing pinned mutable references
to the dynamic future type, as in Listing 17-19.
