Listing 17-33: Using the rx receiver as a ReceiverStream
First, we create a function called get_messages that returns impl Stream<Item = String> . For
its implementation, we create an async channel, loop over the first 10 letters of the English
alphabet, and send them across the channel.
We also use a new type: ReceiverStream , which converts the rx receiver from the
trpl::channel into a Stream with a next method. Back in main , we use a while let loop
to print all the messages from the stream.
use trpl::{ReceiverStream, Stream, StreamExt};
fn main() {
trpl::run(async {
let mut messages = get_messages();
while let Some(message) = messages.next().await {
println!("{message}");
}
});
}
fn get_messages() -> impl Stream<Item = String> {
let (tx, rx) = trpl::channel();
let messages = ["a", "b", "c", "d", "e", "f", "g", "h", "i", "j"];
for message in messages {
tx.send(format!("Message: '{message}'")).unwrap();
}
ReceiverStream::new(rx)
}
